# =============================================================================
# Workspace root: multi-viewpoint-based-anomaly-detection
#
# What this repo tracks: the multiobserverbility source, its dataset files,
# its run records, and the root orchestration that ties the three projects
# together. Everything a script can regenerate stays out.
# =============================================================================

# --- Sibling projects, cloned by the setup script ----------------------------
# Each is its own repository with its own history; the workspace pins their
# versions in the manifest, never their contents.
/ADKGD/
/KGSAGE/

# --- Archive of the repository this workspace was split out of ---------------
/.git_old_adkgd/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# API keys reach the agents through .env. A template may be committed; a
# filled-in one never can.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editors and operating systems -------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- HPC job output ----------------------------------------------------------
# SLURM writes these beside the submit script on every job.
slurm-*.out
*.err
logs/
*.log

# --- Generated artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
# prepared/ holds what scripts 1 and 2 build: the contaminated graph, the
# ground truth, the trained scorer and its score file. All of it is derived
# from data/ (which IS tracked) by seeded scripts, so the clone stays small
# and every machine regenerates its own -- which is also what keeps a stale
# score file from travelling between machines.
prepared/
checkpoints/
temp/
tmp/
scratch/

# Observation runs. Each project ignores its own runs/ (see its .gitignore):
# most are smoke and setup runs, and they churn every session. Runs worth
# keeping are not reproducible -- the model varies between identical runs --
# so copy those into a tracked evidence/ folder rather than committing the
# whole directory.

# Model weights, wherever they land.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# Google ADK session stores.
.adk/

# --- Retired predecessor projects ---------------------------------------------
# Their code is kept for reference; their run output is not.
/multi-observerbility-AD/runs/
/multiviewpoint-AD-in-KGs/runs/

# --- Reference library --------------------------------------------------------
# ~470 MB of publisher PDFs and working notes. Not redistributable and far too
# large for a clone; back these up outside git.
/docs_v1/
/docs_v2/
/docs_thesis/
/papers/

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored -- do not add these:
#   multiobserverbility-AD-in-KGs/data/   dataset files the pipeline reads;
#                                         tracked so an offline HPC node can
#                                         run straight from the clone
#   evidence/                             curated run records kept as results
# =============================================================================

AusDM/